## 8. Next recommended experiments

### 8.1. AR2.A — external SOTA comparison (priority 1)

```text
Goal: how far is v9.0_best from a published LLVE method on our local pipeline?

Method: download LLVE-STCD pretrained ckpt, run on our 14 SDSD/static_np test
seqs with the same RGB-PSNR uint8 + (matched) inference protocol.

Acceptance:
  - same 14 sequences
  - same frame count and PSNR computation
  - record full-frame vs tiled vs padded inference
  - per-sequence table
  - do NOT claim comparability to LLVE-STCD's 28.93 unless their split is used

Cost: 3-5 h engineering. Bounded effort: stop if env conflicts dominate.
```

### 8.2. v9.3-bigdata — BVI-RLV scale-up (priority 2, deferred)

```text
Goal: does larger paired sRGB video data improve the pixel branch ceiling?

Method: download BVI-RLV, train v9.0 on SDSD + BVI-RLV mix, evaluate on both
test sets and on LLVE-STCD's split if reachable.

Cost: ~1.5 day total (download + dataset code + 7500 iter training).

NOT justified by motion hypothesis (closed by Section 6).
JUSTIFIED by data scale and stronger published baselines.

Defer until note + AR2.A done.
```

### 8.3. Decoder/photometric improvements (priority 3, conditional)

If AR2.A shows we're 3+ dB below external SOTA on the same pipeline, the
remaining lever is the pixel decoder side:

```text
- larger / different pixel decoder backbone (Restormer-XL, ConvNeXt-V2, etc.)
- better photometric loss family
- stronger data augmentation
- try removing some of the auxiliary losses (Retinex compose, L_smooth, dod)
```

These are open exploration only after AR2.A and BVI-RLV are decided.

### 8.4. Explicitly blocked

```text
v9.3-temporal-adapter:    closed by Section 6 (no motion correlation)
v9.3-affinity-loss:       closed by Section 5 (V-JEPA invariance)
v9.3-RAFT-warp-revival:   closed by Section 4 (structural negative)
RAW/event-camera pivot:   v10/v11 territory, not v9
v9.0c (mixed indoor+outdoor as separate from v9.0_mix): already done de facto;
                          v9.0 was always mixed-data, not indoor-only
```

